eringUS Exempt RegularFull timeStateside Exempt 5.2 Assistant Vice President, Enterprise Platforms Engineering Office of the Senior Vice President & Chief Information Officer Exempt, Regular, Full-Time University of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) seeks an experienced servant leader as our next Assistant Vice President, Enterprise Platforms Engineering (AVP). Reporting to the Vice President, Platform Engineering, this AVP is responsible for leading a team of directors overseeing the engineering, modernization, escalated support, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications that enable critical institutional business processes. This role oversees application engineering teams supporting key application domains, including Student Information Systems (SIS), Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP), Electronic Document Management (EDM), Faculty Profile Management, and related services. The AVP collaborates with Business Relationship Managers, Enterprise Architecture, Domain and Solution Architects, Data, Integrations, Cybersecurity, Quality Management, Release Enablement, IT Operations, and business stakeholders to ensure delivery of secure, scalable, and maintainable solutions that support UMGC priorities and operational excellence. Position is hybrid with 2-3 days/week in office. Relocation to the Maryland/DC/Northern Virginia metro area is preferred. Specific responsibilities include but are not limited to: · Enterprise Platforms Strategy, Modernization & Domain Alignment. Partner with enterprise and domain architecture to develop and execute applications strategies and investments across multiple technology domains, initiatives, modernization, and lifecycle plans ensuring alignment with architecture standards, business priorities, cybersecurity requirements, and technology direction. · Engineering, Integration & Solution Delivery. Accountable for high quality, efficient application engineering, testing, and escalated support of enterprise applications, services, workflows, and integrations while following engineering standards, methodologies, and delivery practices that ensure scalability, reliability, and maintainability; also responsible for the enterprise platforms engineering budget. · Management, Operations & Service Excellence. Work with architects to provide guidance on business applications lifecycle planning, Tier 3 operational support, issue resolution, performance optimization, and continuous improvement activities that ensure application reliability, availability, security, and business continuity objectives are achieved. · Engineering Governance & Delivery Performanc e. Partner with domain architects to establish business applications engineering governance and performance measures while collaborating with Quality Management and Release Enablement teams to support effective testing, quality assurance, release readiness, and deployment activities. · Business Partnership, Technology Enablement & Vendor Management. Partner with Business Relationship Managers, Enterprise Architecture, Architects, PMO, business leaders, Data, Integrations, Cybersecurity, and IT Operations to understand requirements, evaluate solutions, manage vendor relationships, and deliver technology that enables UMGC objectives and digital initiatives. · Leadership, Workforce Development & Organizational Effectiveness. Lead and develop application engineering managers, solution architects, and engineers through workforce planning, talent development, succession planning, coaching, performance management, and organizational leadership practices that strengthen engineering maturity and delivery effectiveness. · Technology Policy Advisory. Assist the Information Technology Policy Administrator with UMGC technology policy development and refinement. · Incident & Problem Management Leadershi p. Provide leadership for major incident response, escalation management, and operational resilience. Oversee on-call readiness and coverage for critical off-hours support, and drive post-incident reviews, root cause analysis, problem management, and continuous service improvement. Required education & experience: A demonstrated ability to get things done and deliver results. An earned Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution of higher learning in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, Business, or a related technology discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience; at least 10 years of progressive experience in application development, application engineering, software engineering, systems integration, enterprise platforms, or related disciplines, including seven (7) years leading software development, application engineering, architecture, or technical delivery teams; hands-on experience in software engineering, solution architecture, product engineering, enterprise application integration, cloud and hybrid platforms, and low-code, no-code, open-source, and commercial enterprise technologies; hands-on techno-functional experience managing enterprise resource planning (ERP) solutions, including Human Capital Management (HCM), Finance systems, Student Information Systems (SIS), payment gateways, and related enterprise applications; experience leading application modernization, lifecycle management, API and integration solutions, operational support, and technology delivery initiatives; demonstrated expertise in SDLC, Agile, DevOps, engineering governance, application security, performance optimization, vendor management, and cross-functional collaboration with architecture, data, operations, cybersecurity, quality, and business stakeholders. Preferred education & experience: An earned Master's degree from an accredited institution of higher learning in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, Business, or a related technology discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Senior leadership experience directing managers, engineers, architects, and technical teams in complex enterprise environments. Experience leading implementations of Workday and PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, including large-scale business process transformation and enterprise application deployments. Demonstrated success leading cross-application modernization initiatives spanning ERP, HCM, Finance, Student Information Systems, data, identity, and integration platforms. Experience supporting higher education or similarly complex, regulated organizations; experience with enterprise architecture practices, TOGAF, technology roadmaps, and portfolio planning; demonstrated strengths in executive communication, stakeholder engagement, financial stewardship, organizational leadership, workforce development, strategic execution, and continuous improvement. Professional certifications such as CBAP, PMP, Product Management, SAFe, Agile, TOGAF, cloud, DevOps, or ITIL certifications are desirable. All submissions should include a cover letter and resume. The University of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. UMGC is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. Workplace Accommodations: The University of Maryland Global Campus Global Campus (UMGC) is committed to creating and maintaining a welcoming and inclusive working environment for people of all abilities. UMGC is dedicated to the principle that no qualified individual with a disability shall, based on disability, be excluded from participation in or be denied the benefits of the services, programs, or activities of the University, or be subjected to discrimination. For information about UMGC's Reasonable Workplace Accommodation Policy or to request an accommodation, applicants/candidates can contact Employee Accommodations via email at employee-accommodations@umgc.edu . Benefits Package Highlights: Generous Time Off: Enjoy 22 days of paid vacation, 15 days of sick leave, 3 personal days, and 16 paid holidays (17 during general election years). For part-time employees, time off rates will be prorated based on the number of hours worked. Comprehensive Health Coverage: Access to health care, medical with vision, dental, and prescription plans for both individuals and families, effective from the 1st of the month following your hire date. Insurance Options: Term Life Insurance, Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance, and Long-Term Disability (LTD) Insurance. Part-time employees working less than 0.5 FTE are not eligible for LTD. Flexible Spending Accounts: Available for medical and dependent care expenses. Retirement Plans: Choose between the Optional Retirement Program (ORP) or the Maryland State Retirement and Pension System (MSRPS). Supplemental Retirement Plans: include 401(k), 403(b), 457(b), and various Roth options. The university does not provide matching funds. Tuition Remission: Immediate availability for Regular Exempt Staff. Spouses and dependent children are eligible for undergraduate tuition remission after two years of service. NOTE: For part-time employees (at least 50 percent of the time), tuition remission benefits are prorated. Hiring Range: $220,000.00 - $237,000.00 Apply Join Our Talent Network Aveanna Glassdoor Reviews Rated 3.2 out of 5 stars Reviews and Ratings on \" A friendly environment to work and to learn. \" - Current Employee in Largo, MD"
