d motivated. Responsiveness & Feedback Stay consistently engaged with learners throughout the course by responding to inquiries, returning feedback, and posting final grades within the expected timeframe. Proactive Support & Collaboration Monitor Progress: Use available data tools to track student engagement and conduct proactive outreach to at-risk students. Team Up: Partner with success coaches, academic staff, and portfolio directors to refer struggling students to UMGC support resources. Stay Connected: Participate in UMGC's vibrant faculty community, including the Program Hub and ongoing training. Course Structure & Time Commitment Format: 100% Online & Asynchronous Term Length: 8-week sessions (3-credit courses) Class Size: Typically, 25-35 students (smaller sections for select courses) Time Commitment: The adjunct faculty role requires a substantial commitment throughout the term focusing not only on academic success but also the social, personal, and professional growth of students Minimum Qualifications: Education: Terminal degree in Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Data Analytics, or related field from an accredited institution of higher learning. Experience: 3-5 years of professional experience in Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, and Data Analytics. Legal Status: Applicants must have and be able to maintain their own legal status in the country in which they apply to teach. The Mindset: A deeply student-centered approach rooted in empathy, flexibility, professional integrity, and cultural responsiveness. Preferred Qualifications: Industry Certifications in ML, AI, Data Science from Microsoft, IBM, AWS. Experience teaching adult learners in an online, asynchronous environment. Prior postsecondary teaching experience. Active engagement in your discipline's professional community. Materials needed for submission Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover letter highly preferred Unofficial Transcripts If selected, candidates with international degrees may be 