m Jobs Croughton-United Kingdom Jobs Europe Remote Jobs Fairford-United Kingdom Jobs Garmisch-Germany Jobs Geilenkirchen-Germany Jobs Ghedi-Italy Jobs Grafenwoehr-Germany Jobs Hohenfels-Germany Jobs Illesheim-Germany Jobs Isa-Bahrain Jobs Izmir-Turkey Jobs Kaiserslautern-Kapaun-Germany Jobs Kaiserslautern-Kleber-Germany Jobs Kaiserslautern-Rob-Germany Jobs Kaiserslautern (Staff)-Germany Jobs Kleine Brogel-Belgium Jobs Lajes, Azores-Portugal Jobs Lakenheath-United Kingdom Jobs Landstuhl-Germany Jobs Lisbon-Portugal Jobs Livorno (Camp Darby)-Italy Jobs Manama-Bahrain Jobs Mildenhall-United Kingdom Jobs Moron AB Jobs Muwaffaq Salti Air Base - Jordan Jobs Naples-Italy Jobs Powidz FOS Jobs Poznan FOS Jobs Prince Sultan AB (Al-Kharj) Jobs Ramstein-Germany Jobs Rota-Spain Jobs Schinnen (AFNORTH)-Netherlands Jobs Sembach-Germany Jobs SHAPE-Belgium Jobs Sigonella-Italy Jobs Sinai-North Camp-Egypt Jobs Sinai-South Camp-Egypt Jobs Souda Bay-Greece Jobs Spangdahlem-Germany Jobs Stavanger-Norway Jobs Stuttgart-Boeblingen-Panzer-Germany Jobs Vicenza-Italy Jobs Vilseck-Germany Jobs Volkel-Netherlands Jobs Wiesbaden-Army-Germany Jobs Zagan FOS Jobs Aberdeen Proving Grounds - Aberdeen, MD Jobs Adelphi, MD Jobs Andrews Air Force Base, MD Jobs Annapolis Junction, MD (NSA) Jobs Annapolis, MD Jobs Arizona Jobs Arlington, VA Jobs Arundel Mills - Hanover, MD Jobs Baltimore, MD Jobs Bethesda, MD Jobs California Jobs California, MD Jobs College Park, MD Jobs Crystal City Jobs CSM LaPlata Jobs Dorsey - Elkridge, MD Jobs Eglin Air Force Base - Eglin, FL Jobs Elkridge, MD Jobs Fayetteville, NC Jobs Fort Belvoir - Belvoir, VA Jobs Fort Benning - Fort Benning, GA Jobs Fort Bliss East (Biggs) TX Jobs Fort Campbell, KY Jobs Fort Carson Jobs Fort Carson, CO Jobs Fort Cavazos, TX Jobs Fort Detrick, MD Jobs Fort Drum - Fort Drum, NY Jobs Fort Eisenhower, GA Jobs Fort Eustis Jobs Fort Gordon, GA Jobs Fort Gregg-Adams, VA Jobs Fort Hood, TX Jobs Fort Irwin, Fort Irwin, California Jobs Fort Jackson Education Center - Fort Jackson, SC Jobs Fort Lee, VA Jobs Fort Meade - Fort Meade, MD Jobs Fort Myer - Fort Myer, VA Jobs Fort Story_Online Hybrid Jobs Ft. Bliss, TX Jobs GEICO Plaza Jobs Hagerstown, MD Jobs Hampton, VA Jobs Hawaii Jobs Henderson Hall, Navy Annex Jobs Hickam AFB, HI Jobs Holloman Air Force Base, NM Jobs Honolulu, HI Jobs ICC - Adelphi, MD Jobs Indianapolis, IN (North America) Jobs Jacksonville, FL Jobs JBSA-Fort Sam Houston, TX Jobs JBSA-Lackland, TX Jobs JBSA-Randolph Jobs JEB Little Creek, VA Jobs Joint Base Anacostia – Bolling Jobs Joint Base Lewis McChord, WA Jobs JTC Amman Jobs Killeen, TX Jobs Langley Air Force Base Jobs Langley Air Force Base, Hampton, VA Jobs LaPlata, MD Jobs Largo, MD Jobs Laurel College Center Jobs Laurel, MD Jobs Mayport, FL Jobs MCAS Miramar - San Diego, CA Jobs Mihail Kogalniceanu Air Base (MKAB) Jobs - Minot AFB, ND Jobs Newport News, VA Jobs Norfolk Naval Base - Norfolk, VA Jobs NS Mayport Jobs Odenton, MD Jobs Patrick SFB, FL Jobs Patuxent River Naval Air Station - Patuxent River, MD Jobs Pearl City, HI Jobs Quantico (On-base) - Quantico, VA Jobs Remote Jobs Rockville, MD Jobs San Antonio, TX Jobs San Diego - San Diego, CA Jobs Schofield Barracks, HI Jobs Schriever Space Force Base, CO Jobs - Shaw AFB, SC Jobs Stafford, VA Jobs Thomas Nelson Comm College Jobs Travis Air Force Base, CA Jobs Tripler Army Medical Center, HI Jobs Tucson Jobs Tucson GEICO Jobs Largo, MD Jobs USG - Chicago, IL Jobs USG - Rockville, MD Jobs Vandenberg SFB, CA Jobs Virginia Beach, VA Jobs WA, Joint Base Lewis- McChord (JBLM) Jobs Waldorf, MD Jobs Washington DC Jobs View All Jobs Talent Network Assistant Vice President, Faculty Affairs Job Details Apply Refer a Friend Save Job Back Share This Job Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email Job Ref: 10026333 Location: Yokota Headquarters-Japan Category: Advising and Enrollment Type: Full time Assistant Vice President, Faculty Affairs Office of the Vice President & Deputy Director Asia Overseas Regular, Full-time Our administrative offices in Asia, and this position, are located at Yokota Air Base, Tokyo Prefecture, Japan and require relocation. University of Maryland Global Campus in Asia seeks an Assistant Vice President for Faculty Affairs. Reporting directly to the Associate Vice President/Associate Dean and as part of Asia's senior leadership team, the Assistant Vice President, Faculty Affairs (AVP) will be adept at collaborating with peers to address shared needs and solve common problems. The AVP will also effectively liaise with other units across the division and University to support the work of the division and to advance UMGC academic priorities. The Assistant Vice President will collaborate closely with the Chief Learning Experience and Success Officer (CLESO) and cross-functional teams across the University, including the Global Academic and Learning Enterprise (GALE), the Faculty Affairs and Scheduling Team (FAST), and Learning Experience Design (LED) to support faculty success, instructional excellence, and student outcomes. At the direction of the Associate Vice President/Associate Dean, the AVP is responsible for implementation and administration of assigned UMGC (and, if applicable, partnership) degree programs and faculty in accordance with the policies, procedures, and standards of each University and in accordance with the provisions of the military contracts. The AVP will recruit, hire, train, supervise, evaluate, and support both faculty and staff as assigned; oversee programs of study and course selection; as well as provide ongoing staff and faculty mentoring and development. The AVP is the deputy administrator for providing leadership and mentoring of faculty and staff offered by the UMGC Asia division. At the direction of the Associate Vice President/Associate Dean, the AVP will represent UMGC in Asia in global operations and provide creative and innovative solutions for growing established programs and starting new programs. The AVP is a highly visible position within headquarters, at all bases in the division, and with assigned faculty. The AVP will embrace the vision of creating a vibrant academic community of teaching professors and will work with faculty and staff to provide the best possible student experience at UMGC. Specific responsibilities include: Serves as deputy to the division's Associate Vice President/Associate Dean Ensures accountability for regular and ongoing review and support of assigned faculty teaching Manages assigned faculty and ensures quality standards for academic curriculum and programs Ensures quality of course delivery to include, but not limited to faculty recruitment, faculty development, and syllabi review Provides administrative oversight of all faculty in the division Evaluates faculty performance and provides effective feedback and coaching Evaluates faculty course clearances Serves as initial investigator concerning student grievances and academic integrity issues Supervises peer mentoring program Supervises graduate and special programs Reviews faculty course and schedule assignments in collaboration with Assistant VP, Enrollment Operations Supports academic courses and all programs offered in the assigned overseas division Collaborates with the Director, Academic Operations and Student Services, and other university units to provide academic support to the Associate Vice President/Associate Dean (e.g., grade appeals, student complaints, curricular issues, faculty rank and promotion, course evaluations, graduate programs, and other academic initiatives and projects) Ensures that assigned faculty understand our mission and adhere to policy and procedures to support student learners Provides faculty with ongoing opportunities for engagement in curricular initiatives Coordinates and administers all assigned academic programs Acts as a team-player and self-starter with the ability to confidently complete leadership duties as described Coordinates, at the direction of the Associate Vice President/Associate Dean, the submission of proposals with UMGC and partners for curriculum additions, changes, and deletions Collaborates with academic units across the University, including CLESO, GALE, FAST,LED, and other University stakeholders to support faculty development, instructional modalities, academic quality, and student success initiatives. Serves as a key liaison between UMGC in Asia Academic Affairs and university units to ensure alignment of divisional faculty initiatives with institutional priorities related to teaching excellence, learner engagement, and instructional innovation. Provides leadership for faculty development initiatives, including professional learning opportunities that support effective teaching across instructional modalities and emerging pedagogical practices. Performs other job-related duties as assigned Required education & experience: A demonstrated ability to get things done. An earned Master's degree from a U.S. regionally accredited institution of higher learning or a foreign degree equivalent; seven (7) years of experience in higher education including in the field of collegiate teaching; demonstrated experience supervising faculty; strong and articulate communicator with clear and effective verbal and written communication skills, an enthusiastic supporter of adult education within the U.S. military community; adaptable, able to influence key stakeholders, negotiate, and solve problems; the ability to use UMGC systems and the University learning management system (LEO) and competency-based (ELM) programs; and proven experience exercising discretion, confidentiality, as well as the ability to consistently demonstrate organizational and analytical skills. Preferred education & experience: An earned doctoral degree from a U.S. regionally accredited institution of higher learning as well as graduate administration and teaching experience. WHO MAY APPLY: Applicants with individual logistical support (ILS) preferred. Applicant must qualify for ILS. Criteria under which applicants qualify for ILS are: must serve the U.S. Forces exclusively; are not stateless persons; and are not ordinarily resident in the host nation. All submissions should include a cover letter and resume . The University of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. UMGC is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. Workplace Accommodations: The University of Maryland Global Campus Global Campus (UMGC) is committed to creating and maintaining a welcoming and inclusive working environment for people of all abilities. UMGC is dedicated to the principle that no qualified individual with a disability shall, based on disability, be excluded from participation in or be denied the benefits of the services, programs, or activities of the University, or be subjected to discrimination. For information about UMGC's Reasonable Workplace Accommodation Policy or to request an accommodation, applicants/candidates can contact Employee Accommodations via email at employee-accommodations@umgc.edu . Benefits Package Highlights: Generous Time Off: Enjoy between 15 and 22 days of paid vacation, depending on years of service and position. Additionally, 15 days of sick leave, 3 personal days, and 11 paid Federal holidays. For part-time employees, time off rates will be prorated based on the number of hours worked. Comprehensive Health Coverage: Access to health care, medical with vision, dental, and prescription plans for both individuals and families, effective from the 1st of the month following your hire date. Insurance Options: Term Life Insurance, Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance, and Long-Term Disability (LTD) Insurance. Flexible Spending Accounts: Available for medical and dependent care expenses. Retirement Plans: Choose between the Optional Retirement Program (ORP) or the Maryland State Retirement and Pension System (MSRPS). Supplemental Retirement Plans: include 403(b), 457(b), and various Roth options. The university does not provide matching funds. Tuition Remission: Immediate availability for Regular Exempt Staff. Spouses and dependent children are eligible for undergraduate tuition remission after two years of service. NOTE: For part-time employees (at least 50 percent of the time), tuition remission benefits are prorated. Moving Allowances: May be available based on terms, conditions, and agreements of the position. For additional information see: UMGC Benefits Overview for Overseas Regular Employees Hiring Range: $110,000.00 - $130,000.00 Additional Compensation: Employees receive the applicable currency adjustment (CAX) subject to monthly DoD COLA Index for the work location, which is subject to change and fluctuation based on market indices. Apply Join Our Talent Network Aveanna Glassdoor Reviews Rated 3.2 out of 5 stars Reviews and Ratings on \" A friendly environment to work and to learn. \" - Current Employee in Largo, MD"
