nter - Fort Jackson, SC Jobs Fort Lee, VA Jobs Fort Meade - Fort Meade, MD Jobs Fort Myer - Fort Myer, VA Jobs Fort Story_Online Hybrid Jobs Ft. Bliss, TX Jobs GEICO Plaza Jobs Hagerstown, MD Jobs Hampton, VA Jobs Hawaii Jobs Henderson Hall, Navy Annex Jobs Hickam AFB, HI Jobs Holloman Air Force Base, NM Jobs Honolulu, HI Jobs ICC - Adelphi, MD Jobs Indianapolis, IN (North America) Jobs Jacksonville, FL Jobs JBSA-Fort Sam Houston, TX Jobs JBSA-Lackland, TX Jobs JBSA-Randolph Jobs JEB Little Creek, VA Jobs Joint Base Anacostia – Bolling Jobs Joint Base Lewis McChord, WA Jobs JTC Amman Jobs Killeen, TX Jobs Langley Air Force Base Jobs Langley Air Force Base, Hampton, VA Jobs LaPlata, MD Jobs Largo, MD Jobs Laurel College Center Jobs Laurel, MD Jobs Mayport, FL Jobs MCAS Miramar - San Diego, CA Jobs Mihail Kogalniceanu Air Base (MKAB) Jobs - Minot AFB, ND Jobs Newport News, VA Jobs Norfolk Naval Base - Norfolk, VA Jobs NS Mayport Jobs Odenton, MD Jobs Patrick SFB, FL Jobs Patuxent River Naval Air Station - Patuxent River, MD Jobs Pearl City, HI Jobs Quantico (On-base) - Quantico, VA Jobs Remote Jobs Rockville, MD Jobs San Antonio, TX Jobs San Diego - San Diego, CA Jobs Schofield Barracks, HI Jobs Schriever Space Force Base, CO Jobs - Shaw AFB, SC Jobs Stafford, VA Jobs Thomas Nelson Comm College Jobs Travis Air Force Base, CA Jobs Tripler Army Medical Center, HI Jobs Tucson Jobs Tucson GEICO Jobs Largo, MD Jobs USG - Chicago, IL Jobs USG - Rockville, MD Jobs Vandenberg SFB, CA Jobs Virginia Beach, VA Jobs WA, Joint Base Lewis- McChord (JBLM) Jobs Waldorf, MD Jobs Washington DC Jobs View All Jobs Talent Network Writing and Speech, Andersen Air Force Base, The Undergraduate School - Adjunct Faculty Job Details Apply Refer a Friend Save Job Back Share This Job Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email Job Ref: 10025497 Location: Andersen Air Force Base-Guam Category: Adjunct Faculty Type: Part time Adjunct Faculty Writing and Speech The Undergraduate School UMGC Asia Locations: Andersen Air Force Base, Guam This position is specifically to teach on-site at Andersen Air Force Base in Guam. Local applicants only; UMGC does not sponsor logistical support for this role. Applicants must have and be able to maintain their own legal status in the country in which they apply to teach. Some teaching locations may not be accessible by public transportation. Candidates must be able to reliably travel to assigned work locations and perform on-site responsibilities as required. Please visit the following link to learn more about the Writing and Speech courses offered: Writing - https://asia.umgc.edu/online-degrees/course-information.wrtg Speech - https://asia.umgc.edu/online-degrees/course-information.spch At UMGC, we don't just teach; we empower. Founded in 1947, UMGC is an open-access, minority-serving institution serving over 90,000 nontraditional learners worldwide, including a proud, large military-affiliated population. Our students are mature, highly dedicated, and balancing careers, families, and service. As an Adjunct Faculty member, you are the essential partner helping them bridge the gap between classroom theory and real-world career success. Why Teach with UMGC? Focus on Students, Not Course Design: All courses follow a standardized, pre-designed, unified course model. Standardized rubrics, OER materials, library resources, and digital textbooks are fully provided at no cost to you. You get to focus 100% of your energy on mentoring, facilitating, and providing high-quality feedback—no unpaid course-building required. Ongoing Growth: We invest in you. All newly hired faculty receive comprehensive online orientation, alongside ongoing, cost-free professional development opportunities. The Rhythm of Your Week (Key Responsibilities) Adjunct faculty bring our pre-built curriculum to life through real-world expertise and active mentorship. Classroom Engagement & Presence Be Visible: Maintain an active classroom presence at least 5 days per week, introducing yourself with a welcome announcement and driving discussions. Bridge Theory & Practice: Enrich the pre-built curriculum with your own professional expertise and real-world examples. Build Belonging: Foster an inclusive, culturally responsive environment where adult learners feel supported and motivated. Responsiveness & Feedback Stay consistently engaged with learners throughout the course by responding to inquiries, returning feedback, and posting final grades within the expected timeframe. Proactive Support & Collaboration Monitor Progress: Use available data tools to track student engagement and conduct proactive outreach to at-risk students. Team Up: Partner with success coaches, academic staff, and portfolio directors to refer struggling students to UMGC support resources. Stay Connected: Participate in UMGC's vibrant faculty community, including the Program Hub and ongoing training. Course Structure & Time Commitment Course Delivery: UMGC in Europe and UMGC in Asia offer courses in a variety of instructional formats, including face-to-face instruction, online (asynchronous and/or synchronous), hybrid, and live-streaming, depending on the location and academic program. Term Length: Most courses are delivered in accelerated 8-week sessions. Class Size: Enrollment varies by course and location. Teaching Commitment: The adjunct faculty role requires a substantial commitment throughout the term focusing not only on academic success but also the social, personal, and professional growth of students. Minimum Qualifications: Education: A master's degree in Writing, Speech, Communication Studies or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Experience: Relevant academic and/or professional experience in the field. Legal Status: Applicants must have and be able to maintain their own legal status in the country in which they apply to teach. The Mindset: A deeply student-centered approach rooted in empathy, flexibility, professional integrity, and cultural responsiveness. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching adult learners online (asynchronous and/or synchronous), hybrid, and/or face-to-face learning environments. Prior postsecondary teaching experience. Active engagement in your discipline's professional community. Materials needed for submission: Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover letter highly preferred Unofficial Transcripts If selected, candidates with international degrees may be required to submit a translation/degree evaluation from a NACES approved vendor. All submissions should include a cover letter and resume . The University of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. UMGC is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. Workplace Accommodations: The University of Maryland Global Campus Global Campus (UMGC) is committed to creating and maintaining a welcoming and inclusive working environment for people of all abilities. UMGC is dedicated to the principle that no qualified individual with a disability shall, based on disability, be excluded from participation in or be denied the benefits of the services, programs, or activities of the University, or be subjected to discrimination. For information about UMGC's Reasonable Workplace Accommodation Policy or to request an accommodation, applicants/candidates can contact Employee Accommodations via email at employee-accommodations@umgc.edu . Benefits Package Highlights: Health Coverage: Access to health care, medical with vision, dental, and prescription plans for both individuals and families, effective from the 1st of the month following your hire date. NOTE: Adjuncts are only eligible for State of Maryland benefits. Adjuncts are not eligible for the State of Maryland subsidized rates. Adjuncts would be responsible for the total cost if enrolled. Insurance Options: Term Life Insurance and Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance. Supplemental Retirement Plans : include 403(b), 457(b), and various Roth options. The university does not provide matching funds. For additional information please see: UMGC Benefits Overview for Overseas Adjunct Faculty Hiring Range: Non-PhD: Step 1 $920 - Step 16 $1,193 per credit hour PhD: Step 1 $945 - Step 16 $1,215 per credit hour Apply Join Our Talent Network Aveanna Glassdoor Reviews Rated 3.2 out of 5 stars Reviews and Ratings on \" A friendly environment to work and to learn. \" - Current Employee in Largo, MD"
    },
